{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408068-question-about-foci-and-modifiers","id":1408068,"title":"Question about Foci and modifiers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-13T16:36:25-07:00","id":1408068,"title":"Question about Foci and modifiers","content":"I searched the forum but really couldn't find an answer to what I'm looking for. I do realize part of the answer to this question might be &quot;ST discretion&quot;<br /> <br /> I know a mage needs a foci for each sphere. I'm wondering if when MtA was written if it was imagined that a mage needed all 3 foci (standard, personal and unique) defined for each sphere.<br /> <br /> Also, the modifier chart is a bit vague. If they are casting a multisphere rote is the modifier -per- foci, or if they just use them at all. The later seems weak especially if one or some of those Foci are unique.<br /> <br /> I'm also aware that the rule is you can only modify a roll by +/-3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26363-nyogen","name":"Nyogen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T23:59:32-07:00","id":1408109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408068-question-about-foci-and-modifiers#post1408068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a mage needs a foci for each sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Revised and previous Editions. In M20, a Mage only needs at least 7 initial foci (called instruments in M20) that more depend on your paradigm than your tradition, and they are not tied to spheres - thankfully. Only Specialty and Unique (Personalized in M20) Foci remain tied to spheres there, and they are optional for a Mage to have - which makes way more sense in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Note that in Revised too you don't *need* to use your Specialty focus with a sphere. You can use any of your foci to cast any Magic as long as it makes sense for the character to use a specific focus for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm wondering if when MtA was written if it was imagined that a mage needed all 3 foci (standard, personal and unique) defined for each sphere. </div> </div> </div>As I said, in Revised and previous, yes, you need a focus defined for each sphere. But no matter if Revised or M20, you are not *required* to define personal/Unique foci.<br /> <br /> Note: You only need one focus per effect. When it comes to Specialty/Personal/Unique Foci, to make use of the difficulty decrease this would be the focus that is tied to the main sphere that represents the effect. You need Forces + Prime to toss a fireball, but the main sphere here is Forces, so you need the Forces Specialty/Personal/Unique Focus/Instrument if you want the difficulty reduction. Or when you Teleport somebody - the main focus here is the Correspondence one, since you 'teleport' xyz. So the foci are mostly tied to what you do, not what you do it *on* or *with*.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the modifier chart is a bit vague. If they are casting a multisphere rote is the modifier -per- foci or if they just use them at all. </div> </div> </div>If they use them at all. I'd not call that weak however, as there are many ways to quickly stack the modifiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also aware that the rule is you can only modify a roll by +/-3. </div> </div> </div>Note: +/-3 from the *base* difficulty. This is an important distinction <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> If circumstances like distractions, bad prep, wrong tass or whatever have pushed your difficulty to +2 from base, you can use a mixture of foci, quintessence, taking your time etc. to stack up a cumulative -5 modifier to push that down to -3 from base.<br /> In the end the final diff, for whatever reason, just can not lower than -3 or higher than +3 from base difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-14-2020, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}